      "css": ".ds-neutral{font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;font-size:14px;background:var(--surface,#fffef9);color:var(--ink,#202420);border:1px solid var(--rule,#d7d9ce);border-radius:5px;padding:9px 13px;min-height:40px;cursor:pointer}.ds-neutral:hover{background:var(--rail,#eeeade);border-color:var(--muted,#62695e)}.ds-neutral:active{background:var(--accent-soft,#f3e2cd)}.ds-neutral:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--focus,#9b4708);outline-offset:3px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Search field",
      "kind": "input",
      "refersTo": "input",
      "description": "Native-feeling search on a reading surface.",
      "html": "<input class=\"ds-input\" aria-label=\"Search peers\" placeholder=\"Search peers\" type=\"search\">",
      "css": ".ds-input{font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;font-size:14px;background:var(--surface,#fffef9);color:var(--ink,#202420);border:1px solid var(--rule,#d7d9ce);border-radius:5px;padding:10px 12px;min-height:40px;max-width:100%}.ds-input::placeholder{color:var(--muted,#62695e);opacity:1}.ds-input:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--focus,#9b4708);outline-offset:3px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Active navigation",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "navigation-active",
      "description": "Selected route uses orange wash and quiet icons.",
      "html": "<a class=\"ds-nav\" href=\"#overview\" aria-current=\"page\"><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"7\" height=\"7\" x=\"3\" y=\"3\" rx=\"1\"/><rect width=\"7\" height=\"7\" x=\"14\" y=\"3\" rx=\"1\"/><rect width=\"7\" height=\"7\" x=\"14\" y=\"14\" rx=\"1\"/><rect width=\"7\" height=\"7\" x=\"3\" y=\"14\" rx=\"1\"/></svg>Overview</a>",
      "css": ".ds-nav{font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;font-size:14px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:12px 10px;min-height:44px;border-radius:5px;color:var(--accent,#9b4708);background:var(--accent-soft,#f3e2cd);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none}.ds-nav:hover{background:var(--surface,#fffef9);color:var(--ink,#202420)}.ds-nav:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--focus,#9b4708);outline-offset:3px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Ruled panel",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "panel",
      "description": "A flat section for monitoring data.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-panel\"><h2>Network traffic</h2><p>Observed incoming and outgoing traffic.</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-panel{font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;font-size:14px;background:var(--surface,#fffef9);color:var(--ink,#202420);border:1px solid var(--rule,#d7d9ce);padding:20px 24px}.ds-panel h2{font-size:18px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.4;letter-spacing:-.015em;margin:0}.ds-panel p{font-size:12px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted,#62695e);margin:5px 0 0}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tabular metric",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "metric",
      "description": "Quiet label above a prominent tabular reading.",
      "html": "<dl class=\"ds-metric\"><dt>Block height</dt><dd>890,001</dd><small>Latest observed block</small></dl>",
      "css": ".ds-metric{font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:var(--ink,#202420);margin:0}.ds-metric dt{color:var(--muted,#62695e);font-size:13px;margin-bottom:9px}.ds-metric dd{font-size:26px;font-weight:550;line-height:1.4;letter-spacing:-.02em;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;margin:0}.ds-metric small{display:block;color:var(--muted,#62695e);font-size:12px;line-height:1.5;margin-top:6px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Selected block",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "block-strip-selected",
      "description": "A square block cell with selected state and capacity bar.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-block\" aria-pressed=\"true\"><span>890,001</span><span>Chain tip</span><i aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></button>",
      "css": ".ds-block{font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;font-size:14px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;gap:8px;position:relative;min-width:98px;min-height:72px;text-align:left;border:1px solid var(--accent,#9b4708);border-radius:0;padding:14px 12px;background:var(--accent-soft,#f3e2cd);color:var(--accent,#9b4708);cursor:pointer;transition:background-color 180ms ease-out,color 180ms ease-out}.ds-block>span:first-child{font-weight:600;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-block>span:nth-child(2){font-size:10px;color:var(--accent,#9b4708)}.ds-block i{position:absolute;bottom:0;left:0;height:2px;width:72%;background:var(--accent,#9b4708);opacity:.55}.ds-block:hover{background:var(--accent-soft,#f3e2cd);border-color:var(--accent,#9b4708)}.ds-block:active{background:var(--accent-soft,#f3e2cd)}.ds-block:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--focus,#9b4708);outline-offset:3px}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-block{transition:none}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Country distribution",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "panel",
      "description": "Sorted horizontal bars with country names, exact peer counts, percentages and a separate unknown-country group. Illustrative preview values.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-countries\"><h2>Peers by country</h2><dl><div><dt>United States</dt><dd><span class=\"track\"><i style=\"width:66.7%\"></i></span><span>4</span><span class=\"share\">66.7%</span></dd></div><div class=\"unknown\"><dt>Unknown country</dt><dd><span class=\"track\"><i style=\"width:33.3%\"></i></span><span>2</span><span class=\"share\">33.3%</span></dd></div></dl></section>",
      "css": ".ds-countries{font:14px -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;background:var(--surface,#fffef9);color:var(--ink,#202420);border:1px solid var(--rule,#d7d9ce);padding:20px 24px}.ds-countries h2{font-size:18px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 16px}.ds-countries dl{margin:0}.ds-countries dl>div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(140px,1fr) minmax(0,3fr);gap:24px;align-items:center;padding:16px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule,#d7d9ce)}.ds-countries dd{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:20px;margin:0;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-countries .track{background:var(--rail,#eeeade);height:12px;flex:1}.ds-countries i{display:block;height:100%;background:var(--accent,#9b4708)}.ds-countries .unknown i{background:var(--muted,#62695e)}.ds-countries .share{color:var(--muted,#62695e)}@media(max-width:767px){.ds-countries dl>div{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);gap:10px}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Difficulty period",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "panel",
      "description": "Three tabular readings and an accessible linear progress bar based on validated block height. Mobile stacks progress above the remaining readings; syncing and stale data are identified. Illustrative preview values.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-difficulty\"><h2>Difficulty period</h2><dl><div><dt>Period progress</dt><dd>48.96%</dd></div><div><dt>Blocks remaining</dt><dd>1,029</dd></div><div><dt>Next adjustment height</dt><dd>901,152</dd></div></dl><progress aria-label=\"Period progress\" max=\"2016\" value=\"987\"></progress></section>",
      "css": ".ds-difficulty{font:14px -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;background:var(--surface,#fffef9);color:var(--ink,#202420);border:1px solid var(--rule,#d7d9ce);padding:20px 24px}.ds-difficulty h2{font-size:18px;margin:0 0 20px}.ds-difficulty dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));margin:0 0 20px}.ds-difficulty dt{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted,#62695e)}.ds-difficulty dd{margin:9px 0 0;font-size:26px;font-weight:550;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-difficulty progress{width:100%;height:8px;accent-color:var(--accent,#9b4708)}@media(max-width:767px){.ds-difficulty dl{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:20px}.ds-difficulty dl>div:first-child{grid-column:1/-1}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Mining chart readings",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "panel",
      "description": "Hashrate and difficulty history panels share the range picker and native data table. Current readings precede the plots; hashrate uses solid orange and dashed teal windows with a consistent SI scale. Illustrative preview values.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-mining\"><h2>Estimated network hashrate</h2><p>Network-wide estimates using up to 144 and 1,008 blocks.</p><dl><div><dt>144 blocks</dt><dd>910.00 EH/s</dd></div><div><dt>1,008 blocks</dt><dd>895.00 EH/s</dd></div></dl></section>",
      "css": ".ds-mining{font:14px -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;background:var(--surface,#fffef9);color:var(--ink,#202420);border:1px solid var(--rule,#d7d9ce);padding:20px 24px}.ds-mining h2{font-size:18px;font-weight:600;margin:0}.ds-mining p{font-size:12px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted,#62695e);margin:5px 0 20px}.ds-mining dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));margin:0}.ds-mining dt{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted,#62695e)}.ds-mining dd{margin:9px 0 0;font-size:26px;font-weight:550;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}@media(max-width:767px){.ds-mining dd{font-size:23px}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Protocol publication",
    "overview": "A precise protocol publication made operational. Warm paper and ink, restrained orange, fine rules, and compact native-feeling controls give node readings a clear hierarchy. Charcoal and pale ink retain the same structure in dark mode.\n\nThe system uses the user-approved system sans, tabular figures, and monospace identifiers. Flat, ruled work areas hold substantial data without decorative elevation; motion acknowledges selection rather than introducing content.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm paper and ink; charcoal and pale ink in dark mode.",
      "Flat sections separated by fine rules.",
      "Tabular readings and monospace identifiers.",
      "Functional selection feedback and native-feeling controls."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Semantic Pairing Rule",
        "body": "Switch the complete light/dark token set together. Orange marks actions and selection; success, warning, and danger describe states accompanied by text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Data Legibility Rule",
        "body": "Use tabular figures for readings and monospace for hashes and addresses. Keep descriptive copy in the system sans.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Workspace Rule",
        "body": "Keep monitoring sections flat and ruled. Reserve shadows for the peer dialog and navigation drawer.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do use the semantic theme pairs so light and dark retain the same hierarchy.",
      "Do place labels beside status color and provide legible text alternatives to charts.",
      "Do preserve contained horizontal scrolling for dense tables and the block strip.",
      "Do use the named Data Legibility rule for values and identifiers.",
      "Do retain visible focus outlines and respect reduced motion."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't turn monitoring panels into floating cards; use fine rules and tonal separation.",
      "Don't use animation for chart entrances or continuous decorative effects.",
      "Don't replace monospace identifiers with clipped text that cannot be inspected.",
      "Don't let dense data widen the mobile page."
    ]
  }
}
